  "problem": "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ For all $t\\in Q,$ $t<1.$",
  "worked_solution": "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(t):t<1,\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\u2200t\\in Q,\\,P(t).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u2200t\\in Q,\\,P(t))\u2261\u2203t\\in Q,\\,\u00acP(t).\n$$\n\nFinally, $\u2203t\\in Q,\\,\u00acP(t)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $t\\in Q$ such that $t\\ge 1.$",
